hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22292","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rifaa ibn Shaddad, he said: I used to stand over the head of al-Mukhtar, and when his lying became clear to me, I intended, by Allah, to draw my sword and strike his neck, until I remembered a hadith Amr ibn al-Hamiq narrated to me. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever secures a man upon himself and then kills him, he is given the banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection."
"22293","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Isa al-Qari Abu Umar ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Suddi narrated to us, from Rifaa al-Qitbani, he said: I entered upon al-Mukhtar, and he cast a cushion for me and said: Had not my brother Jibril risen from this, I would have cast it for you. He said: So I wanted to strike his neck, and I remembered a hadith my brother Amr ibn al-Hamiq narrated to me. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whichever believer secures a believer upon his blood and then kills him, I am free of the killer."
"22294","Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to me, from Rifaa ibn Shaddad, he said: I used to stand over the head of al-Mukhtar, and when I knew his lying, I intended to draw my sword and strike his neck, then I remembered a hadith Amr ibn al-Hamiq narrated to us. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever secures a man upon himself and then kills him, he is given the banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection."
"22295","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq al-Khuzai, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: If Allah wants good for a servant, He employs him. It was said: And what is His employing him? He said: He opens for him righteous work before his death until those around him are pleased with him."
